---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import DotDivider from "../components/DotDivider.astro";
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Markly Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy for the Markly link saving and bookmark application."
>
  <main class="home-page">
    <section class="hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="hero-title">Markly Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="hero-text">Last updated: September 2026</p>
    </section>

    <DotDivider />

    <section class="policy-grid">
      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Overview</h2>

        <p>
          Markly is a Voxiverse link saving and bookmark application designed to
          help you save, organize, annotate, manage, and return to content you
          discover across the web.
        </p>

        <p>
          This Privacy Policy explains the types of information Markly may
          process, why that information is used, and how information associated
          with your use of Markly is handled.
        </p>

        <p>
          Your privacy matters to Voxiverse. Information processed through
          Markly is used to provide, maintain, secure, support, and improve the
          application and its features.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Information You Create</h2>

        <p>
          Markly stores information you intentionally create or save while using
          the application. This can include bookmarks, URLs, titles,
          descriptions, tags, notes, favorites, pinned items, archived items,
          folders, collections, and other organizational information associated
          with your saved content.
        </p>

        <p>
          Markly may also store images or other visual information associated
          with bookmarks, such as website icons and thumbnails, when those
          features are available.
        </p>

        <p>
          This information is processed so Markly can provide its bookmark
          management, organization, search, display, synchronization, and related
          functionality.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Bookmark & Link Information</h2>

        <p>
          When you save a link, Markly processes the URL and information
          associated with that bookmark so it can be stored and displayed within
          your collection.
        </p>

        <p>
          Depending on the information available for a saved page, bookmark
          information may include the page title, URL, website or host name,
          description, icon, thumbnail, and other publicly available metadata
          associated with the linked page.
        </p>

        <p>
          Information you manually add to a bookmark, including tags and notes,
          is also stored as part of that bookmark.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Folders, Collections & Notes</h2>

        <p>
          Markly provides organizational features that allow bookmarks to be
          placed into folders and collections and associated with notes or other
          information.
        </p>

        <p>
          Information you create through these features, including folder names,
          collection names, collection notes, bookmark notes, ordering
          information, and relationships between bookmarks and collections, may
          be stored as part of your Markly data.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Account Information</h2>

        <p>
          Markly supports account functionality for features such as
          cross-device synchronization. When you sign in, Markly may process
          information associated with your account, including an account
          identifier, email address, display name, authentication provider,
          profile information, and account creation information.
        </p>

        <p>
          The exact information available to Markly depends on the authentication
          method you use and the information you choose or authorize the
          authentication provider to provide.
        </p>

        <p>
          Account information is used to authenticate you, associate your Markly
          data with your account, maintain your signed-in state, and provide
          account-related features.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Sign in with Apple</h2>

        <p>
          Markly currently supports Sign in with Apple. When you choose to sign
          in using Apple, authentication is handled through Apple's
          authentication services.
        </p>

        <p>
          Markly may receive information authorized through Sign in with Apple,
          such as your Apple user identifier, name, and email address. Apple may
          allow you to use features such as Hide My Email, in which case Markly
          may receive an Apple-provided relay email address rather than your
          personal email address.
        </p>

        <p>
          Apple's handling of information through Sign in with Apple is governed
          by Apple's own privacy policies and terms.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Cross-Device Synchronization</h2>

        <p>
          When you use supported account and synchronization features, Markly
          may process and synchronize application data so your information can
          remain available across supported devices.
        </p>

        <p>
          Synchronized information may include account information, bookmarks,
          bookmark details, folders, collections, notes, settings, and other
          information necessary to maintain your Markly experience across
          devices.
        </p>

        <p>
          Synchronization requires information to be transmitted between your
          device and the services used to provide synchronization.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Activity Information</h2>

        <p>
          Markly may maintain activity information related to actions performed
          within the application. This information may be used to provide
          activity history, statistics, organizational features, or other
          user-facing information about your use of Markly.
        </p>

        <p>
          Activity information is associated with functionality inside Markly
          and is not used to create third-party advertising profiles.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>App Settings</h2>

        <p>
          Markly may store preferences and settings you select while using the
          application. These settings are used to preserve your preferred
          experience and configure supported Markly features.
        </p>

        <p>
          Settings may be stored locally on your device or synchronized when
          necessary to provide supported account and cross-device features.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Bug Reports, Ideas & Feedback</h2>

        <p>
          Markly may provide tools that allow you to submit bug reports, feature
          requests, ideas, beta feedback, attachments, and other information to
          Voxiverse.
        </p>

        <p>
          When you intentionally submit a report, the information included in
          that submission may be transmitted to and retained by Voxiverse so the
          report can be received, reviewed, investigated, organized, responded
          to, and updated.
        </p>

        <p>
          Submitted information may include the details you enter into the
          report, selected report categories, attachments you choose to provide,
          technical information included with the submission, and information
          necessary to identify and track the report.
        </p>

        <p>
          Please avoid including passwords, authentication credentials, or other
          highly sensitive personal information in reports or attachments.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Third-Party Websites</h2>

        <p>
          Markly is designed to save and organize links to content available on
          the web. These links may lead to websites, applications, services, and
          content operated by third parties.
        </p>

        <p>
          When you open a saved link and leave Markly to visit a third-party
          website or service, that third party may collect information according
          to its own privacy practices.
        </p>

        <p>
          Voxiverse does not control the privacy practices, content, security, or
          data collection practices of websites and services operated by third
          parties.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>How Information Is Used</h2>

        <p>
          Information processed through Markly may be used to provide and
          maintain the application, save and organize your bookmarks, maintain
          your account, synchronize supported data, preserve your preferences,
          provide activity features, respond to reports and feedback, diagnose
          technical problems, protect the application, and improve Markly.
        </p>

        <p>
          Voxiverse does not use the contents of your personal bookmark
          collection to build advertising profiles about you.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Advertising & Tracking</h2>

        <p>
          Voxiverse does not sell your Markly bookmark collection, notes, tags,
          folders, collections, or other saved content to advertisers.
        </p>

        <p>
          Markly does not use your saved-link activity to track your browsing
          behavior across unrelated third-party websites for targeted
          advertising purposes.
        </p>

        <p>
          Saving a link in Markly does not give Voxiverse control over tracking
          or advertising technologies that may be used by the third-party
          website when you later visit that website.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Sharing of Information</h2>

        <p>
          Information may be processed by service providers or platform services
          when necessary to operate features such as authentication,
          synchronization, infrastructure, or other functionality required by
          Markly.
        </p>

        <p>
          Information may also be disclosed when required by applicable law,
          legal process, or a valid governmental request, or when reasonably
          necessary to protect the security, rights, and integrity of Markly,
          Voxiverse, or its users.
        </p>

        <p>
          Voxiverse does not sell your personal information or personal Markly
          content to third parties.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Data Storage & Security</h2>

        <p>
          Markly uses reasonable technical and organizational safeguards
          intended to protect information against unauthorized access,
          alteration, disclosure, loss, or misuse.
        </p>

        <p>
          Some information may be stored locally on your device, while
          information associated with account, synchronization, support, or
          other connected features may be processed through services required to
          provide those features.
        </p>

        <p>
          No method of electronic storage or transmission can be guaranteed to
          be completely secure, and absolute security cannot be guaranteed.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Data Retention</h2>

        <p>
          Markly information may be retained for as long as necessary to provide
          the application and the features you use, maintain your account,
          preserve synchronized information, resolve reports, comply with legal
          obligations, and protect the security and integrity of Voxiverse
          services.
        </p>

        <p>
          Information that you remove from the application may not disappear
          immediately from backups, synchronized systems, or records that must
          temporarily be retained for legitimate operational, security, or legal
          purposes.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Deleting Your Content</h2>

        <p>
          Markly provides controls for managing the content you create within the
          application. You may delete bookmarks and other supported information
          when you no longer want it in your Markly collection.
        </p>

        <p>
          Deleting content may also affect relationships with folders,
          collections, notes, or other organizational information associated
          with that content.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Your Choices</h2>

        <p>
          You control the links and organizational content you choose to save in
          Markly, the notes and tags you create, the information you submit
          through feedback and reporting tools, and whether you use optional
          account features where available.
        </p>

        <p>
          You may also choose not to open third-party websites saved within your
          collection or remove links you no longer wish to keep.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>

        <p>
          Markly is not designed to knowingly collect personal information from
          children in violation of applicable privacy laws.
        </p>

        <p>
          If Voxiverse becomes aware that personal information has been
          collected in circumstances requiring parental consent or deletion
          under applicable law, appropriate steps will be taken to address that
          information.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Changes to Markly</h2>

        <p>
          Markly will continue to develop over time. New features or services may
          change the types of information required to provide the application or
          the ways existing information is processed.
        </p>

        <p>
          When changes materially affect the information described in this
          Privacy Policy, this policy may be updated to reflect those changes.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>

        <p>
          This Privacy Policy may be updated from time to time to reflect changes
          to Markly, Voxiverse services, legal requirements, security practices,
          or the ways information is processed.
        </p>

        <p>
          When this policy is updated, the revised version will be published on
          this page and the last updated date will be changed accordingly.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Terms of Service</h2>

        <p>
          Your use of Markly is also governed by the Markly Terms of Service.
          The Terms explain the rules and conditions that apply when accessing
          or using the application.
        </p>

        <p>
          <a href="/legal/markly/terms" class="policy-link">
            View Markly Terms of Service
          </a>
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Contact</h2>

        <p>
          If you have questions about this Privacy Policy, your information, or
          how Markly handles information, you can contact Voxiverse.
        </p>

        <p>
          <a href="/contact" class="contact-button">Contact</a>
        </p>
      </article>
    </section>
  </main>
</DocsLayout>

<style>
  .policy-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(320px, 1fr));
    gap: 1.25rem;
    padding-bottom: 5rem;
  }

  .policy-card {
    background: var(--surface-standard);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 24px;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    transition:
      transform 0.2s ease,
      border-color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .policy-card:hover {
    transform: translateY(-2px);
    border-color: var(--accent-periwinkle);
  }

  .policy-card h2 {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--heading-small);
  }

  .policy-card p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .policy-card a {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .policy-link {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    color: var(--accent-periwinkle) !important;
  }

  .policy-link:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .contact-button {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 0.75rem 1.25rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--accent-periwinkle);
    color: var(--color-bg);
    border: 1px solid rgba(242, 239, 231, 0.12);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition:
      transform 0.2s ease,
      border-color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .contact-button:hover {
    transform: translateY(-1px);
    border-color: var(--accent-periwinkle);
  }

  @media (max-width: 680px) {
    .policy-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 1rem;
    }

    .policy-card {
      padding: 1.25rem;
      border-radius: 20px;
    }
  }
</style>